    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a6">

                <pb facs="0193" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg89"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 243.—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain Pitts to Mr. Hosmer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Champerico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 26, 1890</date>.
                        (Received in Guatemala 5:10 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">James R. Hosmer</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States Consul-General:</hi></p>
                <p>The passenger J. M. Barrundia embarked at Acapulco with a direct ticket for
                    Panama. Under these circumstances, I would suggest, as a guaranty for my ship
                    and myself, to hold the passenger on board until my arrival at San José, where I
                    will place myself under the orders of the American minister. As you expect him
                    this afternoon, please submit this to him and give me an answer.</p>
                <p>Please ask Hockmeyer &amp; Co. for the cipher word in the Pacific Mail code of my
                    name, and insert the same in your answer. Please send man-of-war with your
                    written orders, and avoid telegraphic orders, if possible. Answer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. G. Pitts.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
